Chapter: BvtLodgeBar
  cites Uoaix chapter CityWorkers
  cites Uoaix chapter CompositeFighter
  cites Uoaix chapter BritainShopHours
  cites Uoaix chapter BvtCheck

 UOAIX-260: a shop that lodges workers is not barred at night (bsh-lodges, left out of the door rows by bsh-shop-of),
 since trial 44158's reagent gatherers could not reach their beds in the herbalist's building from hour 19 to 7. The
 set is the lodging data: Britain's reagent gatherers' inn is the herbalist's premises, the hunter's lodge is the
 tanner, and no other shop lodges.
  blb-count : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  blb-count (i) (n) = if i >= bb-shop-count then n else blb-count (i + 1) (n + (if bsh-lodges i then 1 else 0))
  bvt-lodge-bar : Integer -> [Console] Integer
  bvt-lodge-bar (unused) = act
    c <- cw-britain
    herb <- list-at bb-shops bb-herbalist
    a <- bvt-check "the herbalist's building lodges Britain's reagent gatherers and is not barred at night (UOAIX-260)" (c.inn.x1 == herb.x1 & c.inn.y1 == herb.y1 & bsh-lodges bb-herbalist)
    b <- bvt-check "the tannery lodges the hunter and is not barred at night (UOAIX-260)" (cgh-profile.lodge == bb-tanner & bsh-lodges bb-tanner)
    d <- bvt-check ("no other shop is kept unbarred: " & show (blb-count 0 0) & " lodging shops") (blb-count 0 0 == 2 & not (bsh-lodges bsh-inn) & not (bsh-lodges 0))
    a + b + d
  end
